# VARZISH.pni
# PANINI Source Representation
# Canonical Working Specification
# Humanesque / Zistgah
# Status: Canonical working specification
# Principle: RETRIEVE, DON'T RECONSTRUCT

TITLE: VARZISH
SUBTITLE: The Experience–Assessment–Production Environment
ROLE: Zistgah learning-execution / practice-development layer
CORE PRINCIPLE: Do not automate away the developmental process.
AUTOMATION PRINCIPLE: Automate construction, orchestration, observation and adaptation of the developmental process while keeping expert correction inside the architecture.

---

## 1. CONSTITUTIONAL POSITION

VARZISH is the practice, development, assessment, simulation and production environment through which capability is developed, exercised, evidenced, corrected and advanced.

FAKIR -> retrieves domainal reality
FAKIR -> locates mission
FAKIR -> identifies domain(s)
FAKIR -> permits composite domainal configurations
FAKIR -> retrieves/orients toward appropriate VARZISH

FAKIR = WHERE / WHAT DOMAINAL REALITY
VARZISH = HOW CAPABILITY IS DEVELOPED, EXERCISED AND EVIDENCED WITHIN THAT DOMAIN

Varzish is not merely:
- an LMS
- a course catalogue
- a quiz engine
- a credential generator
- a static content repository

Varzish is the Experience–Assessment–Production Environment.

Varzish may encompass:
- practices
- disciplines
- methods
- traditions
- techniques
- institutions
- knowledge

Invariant:
RETRIEVE, DON'T RECONSTRUCT.

